HOW TO ADD A NEW TEST CLASS
────────────────────────────
1. Create YourTests.java in src/test/java/tests/ extending BaseTest
2. Copy a <test> block below, rename it, and fill in your class name
3. Save — Maven will pick it up on the next `mvn test`

HOW TO SKIP A TEST CLASS TEMPORARILY
──────────────────────────────────────
Wrap the <test> block in a comment.

HOW TO RUN SPECIFIC METHODS ONLY
──────────────────────────────────
    <test name="Registration and Login Tests">
        <classes>
            <class name="tests.RegisterLoginTests">
                <methods>
                    <include name="TC01_registerNewUser"/>
                    <include name="TC02_loginWithValidCredentials"/>
                </methods>
            </class>
        </classes>
    </test>

HOW TO RUN IN PARALLEL (methods)
──────────────────────────────────
Each @Test gets its own browser via @BeforeMethod, so parallel-by-methods
is safe without any code changes. Just add to the <suite> tag:
    parallel="methods" thread-count="4"
-->

